			"createdAt": "2020-12-13T22:08:22Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533",
			"summary": "The opener asks whether supporting line and pie charts alongside the default bar chart justifies the added complexity, and offers two implementations: keep the raw data so the chart type can be switched later, or ask for the chart type before the elements are inserted.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjMwMjE5MjUz",
			"actorType": "human"
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTQx",
			"kind": "comment",
			"actor": "lipis",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-14T13:49:28Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-204941",
			"summary": "A maintainer finds line charts appealing but warns pie charts need many colours and labels, and argues against both a paste-time prompt and stored chart metadata since nothing supports them yet.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY3Ng==",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDEwOkRpc2N1c3Npb242NjQxOQ=="
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTU0",
			"kind": "reply",
			"actor": "dwelle",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-14T13:52:52Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-204954",
			"summary": "A second maintainer suggests a 'paste special' context-menu submenu listing chart types, which avoids storing metadata because converting an existing chart would not be supported.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTM4NDY=",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTQx"
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA1MDEy",
			"kind": "reply",
			"actor": "lipis",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-14T14:11:13Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-205012",
			"summary": "The first maintainer notes the app cannot tell whether the clipboard holds chart data until the user pastes, so such a menu item cannot be shown selectively.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY3Ng==",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTQx"
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA1MDIz",
			"kind": "reply",
			"actor": "dwelle",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-14T14:17:17Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-205023",
			"summary": "The second maintainer replies that the newer Clipboard API can read on right-click, but new users would then see a permission prompt when opening the menu.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTM4NDY=",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTQx"
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA1MDY2",
			"kind": "reply",
			"actor": "dwelle",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-14T14:24:18Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-205066",
			"summary": "The second maintainer adds that the menu could appear only when clipboard permission is already granted, while admitting the UX cost and limited browser support.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTM4NDY=",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjA0OTQx"
		},
		{
			"id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50MjE3NzY5",
			"kind": "comment",
			"actor": "andyczerwonka",
			"createdAt": "2020-12-17T00:54:14Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/discussions/2533#discussioncomment-217769",
			"summary": "A user says charts without at least simple grouping will stay a novelty and backs storing the raw data so types can be switched.",
			"actorId": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg5OA==",
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "MDEwOkRpc2N1c3Npb242NjQxOQ=="
		},
		{
